  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Blended Finance Investor Engagement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT&apos;s Development Finance Review recognised opportunity to mobilise significant financing from philanthropic organisations, impact and institutional investors to respond to development and climate challenges in our region. This investment responds recommendation 7 of the review to enhance engagement and collaboration with the private finance community. The investment includes a partnership with the Australian Sustainable Finance Institute to draw institutional investment into development and positive climate outcomes in the Indo-Pacific. It also includes technical and investor relationship support for DFAT&apos;s International Development Investor Group which will draw in co-investment from Australian impact investors into DFAT&apos;s pipeline of climate, gender equality and development investment opportunities in the Indo Pacific. It will also support research and representation opportunities with the aim of drawing in private investment for development climate and gender equality outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
